# H1 `jobctl` and `signal`: real stops and continues, with the binary in a
# foreground group of its own. Ctrl-Z first -- the binary's own suspend, its
# restore and then a SIGTSTP it raises, which now stops it -- and SIGCONT to
# its pid, as `fg` would send; then a SIGTSTP from outside and SIGCONT again;
# then SIGTERM, with `keep` so the pane's dead status says which signal ended
# it. `wire` after each stop and at the end has the bytes in between.
jobctl
keep
wait 4
snap start
key C-z
wait 1
snap ctrlz
wire ctrlz
signal SIGCONT
wait 1.5
snap ctrlz-continued
signal SIGTSTP
wait 1
snap stopped
wire stopped
signal SIGCONT
wait 1.5
snap continued
type still here
wait 0.7
snap typed
signal SIGTERM
wait 1
snap terminated
wire end
